<title>USA: Hewlett-Packard cuts Ethernet pricing.</title>
<headline>Hewlett-Packard cuts Ethernet pricing.</headline>
<dateline>PALO ALTO, Calif. 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hewlett-Packard Co said Monday it had cut prices up to 42 percent on its Ethernet switching hubs used to link computer local area networks.</p>
<p>The company said price reductions on its AdvanceStack 10Base-T switching hubs price reductions are effective April 1.</p>
<p>As examples, HP's AdvanceStack Hub-8E, an entry-level 10Base-T hub for small, stand-alone networks, will be priced at $179, down from $199.</p>
<p>An AdvanceStack Switching Hub-24T with accompanying management software is now $1,399, down from $1,979.</p>
</text>
